B = [
('Winsor and Newton','Europe','19th century-present','art supplies','In the style of Winsor and Newton, classic British artists heritage in monochrome. Bold black lettering in wide, flared Roman capitals, with an ampersand set small between two stacked words, sits beside a rearing winged griffin crest drawn in fine black line engraving. Palette is ink black, crisp white, cream paper tones and rich deep blue, with a single bold red band as an accent. Surfaces are matte card, silver foil, satin enamel and polished brass with fine rule lines, thin borders and a tagline in small italic serif. Layouts are symmetrical and orderly, scholarly, traditional and quietly prestigious, with a smart craft finish.'),
('Caran d Ache','Europe','1930s-present','art supplies','In the style of Caran d Ache, a precise Swiss spectrum of intense, saturated colour arranged in tidy graded rows. Hexagonal faceted forms carry glossy lacquer in deep tones, and each is dipped at the end in a matching colour. Palette is vivid scarlet, cobalt, emerald, sunflower yellow and violet, set against dark charcoal, matte black and bright white. Metal surfaces are gold, silver, anodised and satin, with sharp chiselled edges and fine engraved lines. Lettering is a crisp, upright, widely spaced sans-serif in white or gold, with a small mountain-like emblem and a red square mark. Luxurious, exact, jewel-like and colourful.'),
('Moleskine','Europe','1990s-present','stationery','In the style of Moleskine, sober, understated and travel-worn elegance. Surfaces are matte black, oilcloth-like and softly pebbled, with gently rounded corners, a single elastic closure band and a thin ribbon accent. Palette is black, cream and ivory, with bright flat accent colours such as vermilion, teal, sage green, mustard and navy used one at a time in solid fields. Sewn construction and visible stitching show honest craft. A narrow paper band wraps the outside with small printed text. Lettering is a clean, light, spaced sans-serif, often in tiny size, with a blocky square logo mark. Neat, minimal, modern, with soft ivory tone.'),
('Pelikan','Europe','1930s-present','stationery','In the style of Pelikan, confident German heritage in royal blue and white. Lettering is a bold, rounded, italic-leaning blue wordmark, paired with a circular emblem showing a nesting bird in a simple, strong silhouette. Palette is deep ultramarine, snow white and black, with classic green, cream and tortoiseshell amber stripes and gold-coloured trim for premium looks. Materials are glossy resin, striped celluloid-like patterns, polished gold finish, fine engraved scrollwork and clean enamel. Forms are plump, rounded and smoothly tapered with generous proportions. Later pieces use playful bright colour-blocked stripes. Reliable, traditional, handsome and well made, with crisp white and blue surfaces.'),
('Rotring','Europe','1950s-present','stationery','In the style of Rotring, precision drafting sensibility from Germany. A signature red ring and a bold lowercase red wordmark with a circle-and-bar motif form the mark, always set on black, white or grey. Palette is matte black, brushed steel, silver, graphite and one vivid scarlet accent. Surfaces are knurled, crosshatched metal with fine machined ridges, satin anodised finishes and tiny white printed scale markings. Forms are hexagonal, cylindrical and tapered, slim and tool-like, with crisp edges and no ornament. Lettering is small, geometric and technical, with thin red rings and numerals. Engineered, exact, draughtsman-like, serious and timeless.'),
('Steinway and Sons','North America','1880s-present','musical instruments','In the style of Steinway and Sons, formal grandeur in black and gold. A mirror-bright black lacquer finish has deep, flawless reflections and sweeping, flowing curves. Gold appears as a small lyre emblem with a decorative harp-like outline, and in widely spaced, thin serif capitals reading the name. Alternate finishes include dark mahogany, burl walnut, ebony and ivory-white with warm satin sheen. Details use polished brass, gilded cast ornament and tapered, turned supports with subtle carving. Palette is black, gold, ivory and rich dark wood. Restrained, noble, symmetrical and timeless, with a refined, expensive hush.'),
('Martin Guitars','North America','1830s-present','musical instruments','In the style of Martin Guitars, old-world American craftsmanship in warm wood. Honey-gold spruce tone ages to amber, paired with deep brown rosewood, mahogany and dark ebony. Decoration is delicate and hand-made, with herringbone inlay bands, fine concentric rings, cream edge trim, tortoiseshell accents and mother-of-pearl in flowing vine, snowflake and floral patterns. Lettering is a vintage mix of looping script initial letters and tall, narrow capitals with an established-year line, in gold, cream or pearl. Finishes are thin satin to soft gloss lacquer, naturally crackled with age. Palette is amber, cream, brown and black. Traditional, tender, heirloom and honest.'),
('Gretsch Guitars','North America','1950s-present','musical instruments','In the style of Gretsch Guitars, flashy mid-century American showmanship. Finishes are deep orange lacquer, cherry red, pearl white, two-tone green and sparkling metallic, all glossy and deep. Gold-plated and chrome accents gleam beside cream and black edge stripes. Lettering is a bold, slanted, italic block script in black or gold with a sharp underline swoosh. Emblems include a circular badge with a stylised letter G and a stylised V shape, with oversized decorative cut-outs. Details are bold stripes, rows of bright studs, striped and sparkle edging, and generous proportions. Palette is orange, gold, cream, black and red. Loud, showy and rockabilly cool.'),
('Rickenbacker','North America','1950s-present','musical instruments','In the style of Rickenbacker, sleek mid-century modern with an art-deco edge. Lettering is a distinctive, long, flowing, slanted script with exaggerated looping tails and a swooping, connected stroke, in black, white or chrome on a triangular, tapered white panel. Finishes are high gloss jetglo black, fireglo red-orange sunburst, mapleglo natural wood, white and bold primary colours. White edge stripes, chrome trim and sharp, angular points give a crisp, futuristic profile. Triangular and slanted shapes recur, with sharply pointed corners and slotted cut-outs. Palette is black, white, chrome and glowing red. Retro, stylish, sharp and jangly cool.'),
('Taylor Guitars','North America','1970s-present','musical instruments','In the style of Taylor Guitars, modern California craftsmanship, clean, bright and precise. Wood is light, finely grained and blond, with koa, sapele and rosewood in rich reddish-brown for contrast. Finishes are very thin, flawless and glossy, with smooth rounded bevelled edges and a sleek, slim, contemporary silhouette. Inlay is minimal, with slender abalone and mother-of-pearl in organic shapes of birds, feathers, vines and leaves, with fine black and cream edge lines. Lettering is a warm, rounded serif wordmark in gold or cream on a red or brown oval badge, with a curved arc of small capitals above it. Palette is honey, caramel, cream, chestnut and burgundy. Friendly, polished and refined.'),
]
